# State holds resource ids and, since F17, the two credential values. Local only (decision Q3).
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
# Every environment's values, filled in from terraform.tfvars.example (README): project id,
# region, bucket names, flags — none of it belongs in git. `pnpm make-credentials` writes
# secrets.auto.tfvars the same way, matched by the `*.auto.tfvars` case below; `*.tfvars`
# alone would already cover it, but the name is kept as documentation of what that file is.
# `terraform.tfvars.example` does not match either pattern (it ends in `.example`, not
# `.tfvars`) and stays tracked.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
*.auto.tfvars
secrets.tfvars
.terraform/
crash.log
*.tfplan
# Names the GCS state bucket for `terraform init -backend-config=backend.hcl` (README,
# "State in a GCS bucket") — project-specific, so it never goes in git either.
backend.hcl
